�In 1942, Executive Order 9066 mandated the incarceration of 110,000 Japanese Americans, including men, women, children, the elderly, and the infirm, for the duration of the war. Allowed only what they could carry, they were given just a few days to settle their affairs and report to assembly centers. Businesses were lost, personal property was stolen or vandalized, and lives were shattered. The Japanese word gaman means "enduring what seems unbearable with dignity and grace. "Imprisoned in remote camps surrounded by barbed wire and guarded by soldiers with machine guns, the internees sought courage and solace in art. Using found materials at first and later what they could order by catalog, they whittled and carved, painted and etched, stitched and crocheted. What they created is a celebration of the nobility of the human spirit under adversity. THE ART OF GAMAN presents more than 150 examples of art created by internees, along with a history of the camps.Reviews". . . demonstrates the poignancy of the internment experience and the strength of the human spirit."-Alaska Airlines Magazine"�
�E sustematike arnese ton pragmatikon aition tes europaikes krises gennese mia titania makhe me thumata ten akeraioteta kai ten psukhe tes Europes. Ste makhe aute ettontai kathemerina oi dunameis tes logikes kai tou anthropismou kai thriambeuoun o autarkhismos, e anisoteta, mia morphe dethen litotetas pou uponomeuei ten idia tes te logike. Os apotelesma, oi phugokentres dunameis pou apodomoun ten Europaike Enose eniskhuontai - me to Brexit na dinei apla progeuse tou ti tha akolouthesei. To apotelesma autes tes titanias sugkrouses okhi mono tha krinei to mellon tes epeirou mas, alla kai tha apodeikhthei krisimo gia ten uphelio. E nike tou orthologismou, tes eleutherias, tes demokratias kai tou anthropismou sten Europe einai, alle mia phora, diakubeuma gia olon ton kosmo.
Sto neo tou biblio, o Gianes Barouphakes aphegeitai te demiourgia tes eurozones pano sta ereipia tou entuposiakou metapolemikou oikonomikou sustematos pou estesan, os epektase tou Niou Ntel, oi epigonoi tou proedrou Rousbelt. Antitheta me ekeine te nomismatike kai oikonomike enose (to Mpreton Gounts), e eurozone oikodometheke sathra, me tropo pou te metetrepse gregora se puramidiko skhema (idiotikou kai demosiou) khreous, me khores opos e Ellada, e Irlandia, e Portogalia kai e Ispania ston rolo tou monimos apheregguou daneiolepte.
To biblio tou Giane Barouphake "E arpage tes Europes" skubei prosektika kai methodika pano sten prosphate europaike mas istoria, parathetontas ephiktes luseis kai anadeiknuontas te metamornterna ekdose tes dekaetias tou 1930 pou karadokei ean kanoume to lathos na pistepsoume pos oi mones mas epiloges einai eite e upotage stis diaphores troikes eite e dialuse tes Europaikes Enoses. (Apo ten parousiase sto opisthophullo tou bibliou)"�
�Modern Chess Openingsis the best and most trusted tool for serious chess players on the market. First published over a half-century ago, this is a completely revised and updated edition of the book that has been the standard English language reference on chess openings. An invaluable resource for club and tournament players, it now includes information on recent matches and the most up-to-date theory on chess openings.
Modern Chess Openings is ideal for intermediate players ready to elevate their game to the next level or International Grandmasters who want to stay on top of recent chess innovations."�
�Panikos katalambanei te souedike koinonia otan o enas meta ton allo dolophonountai oi megaloepikheirematies tes khoras. Prokeimenou na dialeukanthei e upothese to takhutero dunaton kai khoris alles apoleies, o Arkhegos tes Astunomias sustenei ten epilekte Omada Alpha. An kai eterokleto sunolo, e omada kaleitai na sullabei ton <>, pou truponei sta salonia tous khoris na aphenei ikhne, akouei tzaz paramoneuontas sto skotadi kai skotonei panta me duo purobolismous sto kephali. Oi ereunes odegoun se diaphoretikous dromous* apo tis trapezes kai ten istioploIa os te rosike maphia kai enan thruliko autoskhediasmo tou tzazista Telonious Monk ... MisteriosoMe kheirourgike akribeia o Arne Ntal anatemnei te sugkhrone koinonike pragmatikoteta kai graphei ena sphikhto kai sunarpastiko astunomiko muthistorema, to opoio agapetheke apo ekatommuria anagnostes se olo ton kosmo."�
�"To proi tes 9es Martiou 1944, edolophonethe me peristrophon o phoitetes tes Nomikes Aggelos Notaras, eis ton peribolon tes Agias Photeines Ilisou..."
Liga khronia argotera, apo ena aproblepto paikhnidi tes moiras, mia nea kai anesukhe gunaika, e Rode Simonete, anakaluptei te photographia tou Aggelou. To blemma tou te magnetizei. E musteriodes morphe tou te sageneuei. Thelei na mathei ta panta gi' auton. Na anastesei to parelthon tou. Eroteumene pleon mazi tou, xekina enan agona gia na brei ton ekteleste tou. Badizei pano sta matomena ikhne tes Istorias, skalizei mnemes kai arkheia kai apokruptographei methodika ten prosopikoteta tou Aggelou. Me asigasto to pathos tes ereunas, tha gnorisei oneiropolous alla kai dolophonous, agious alla kai amartolous, mekhri pou to nema tes skoteines autes upotheses tha ten odegesei se prosopa kai katastaseis pou den mporouse kan na upopsiastei..."␀␀`@"	
